# MSP-ALIGN release signing keys (2.0), in git's "allowed signers" format:
#   releases@mspalign.org namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... comment
#
# Servers install only release tags (vX.Y.Z) signed with one of these keys, checked against the copy of this file
# they already have. A new key is added by a release signed with a key listed here now, so a stolen GitHub account
# alone can't ship an update. With no key here (a fork, or a development copy), updates follow the branch unsigned.
# See docs/RELEASING.md.
